<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kainji Dam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1968</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kainji Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger River</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, completed in 1968. Its reservoir, Kainji Lake, flooded the old town of Bussa and other settlements, whose people were moved to new towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-bussa">New Bussa</a>. It remains one of the main sources of electricity in Nigeria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kainji-dam.jpg" alt="Kainji Dam" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samuel Ayenajeh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River_Niger_at_Kainji_Dam_Niger_State.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
